ective master's or Ph.D. applicant and interested in applying for an engineering degree, please use the EngineeringCAS application. The general application is not needed.\nSubmit your official transcripts.\nTo be considered official, each transcript must come directly to SDSU from the institution. Student issued transcripts are not considered official.\nRequest official transcripts from:\nEach institution from which a degree was earned or will be earned.\nAny institution at which you have earned graduate credits.\nIf you attended a South Dakota regental institution, the Office of Admissions will access all transcripts for you. You do not need to take any action.\nSubmit any additional documents required by your program of interest.\nIf submitting Graduate Record Examination (GRE) scores, send directly to SDSU from ETS.\nThe SDSU GRE code is 6653.\nFor a program within the Jerome J. Lohr College of Engineering, use GRE code 2862.\nContact ETS for more information about the GRE test.\nDepartmental review.\nWhen all required documents have been received, your application file will be sent to the appropriate department for review. Allow for a minimum of three to four weeks for departmental review. You will receive an email notification of the admission decision.\nContact Us\nOffice of Admissions\nPhysical Address\n1175 Medary Ave.\nBrookings,\nSD\n57007\nMailing Address\nEnrollment Services Center, Box 511\nBrookings,\nSD\n57007\nView Location\nHours\nMon - Fri:\n8:00 a.m.-5:00 p.m.\nEmail\n800-952-3541\nVisit Us\nCome Meet Your Future\nMeet the people that will help shape your future and define your college experience! Learn more about your academic interests with some of our world-class faculty.\nApply Today\nPlan Your Visit\nRequest Info\nStudents\nCost and Aid\nVisiting\nStudent Life\nApplying\nMore Info\nGet Directions\nGive to SDSU\nOffice Directory\nExplore\nAbout SDState\nAcademics\nAdmissions\nStudent Life\nResearch\nCommunity\nConnect\nAlumni\nAthletics\nBooks